            <ArticleTitle>Pelvic floor hypertonic disorders: identification and management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>707-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ogc.2009.08.011</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients with hypertonic pelvic floor disorders can present with pelvic pain or dysfunction. Each of the various syndromes will be discussed including elimination disorders, bladder pain syndrome/interstitial cystitis (BPS/IC), vulvodynia, vaginismus, and chronic pelvic pain. The symptoms and objective findings on physical examination and various diagnostic studies will be reviewed. Therapeutic options including physical therapy, pharmacologic management, and trigger point injections, as well as botulinum toxin injections will be reviewed in detail.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
